## 📌 Project Overview

A comprehensive end-to-end analysis of **U.S. airline flight delays** using 11 years of data (2013–2023) sourced from the Bureau of Transportation Statistics (BTS). The project identifies the root causes of flight delays, ranks airports and carriers by delay volume, uncovers seasonal patterns, and delivers actionable delay-reduction recommendations.

---

## 🎯 Problem Statement

An airline company faces frequent flight delays. The goal is to:

- ✅ Identify the **root causes** of delays (carrier, weather, NAS, late aircraft, security)
- ✅ Rank **airports** by delay severity and volume
- ✅ Analyze **carrier performance** across all 23 U.S. airlines
- ✅ Detect **seasonal and time-based** delay patterns
- ✅ Present **data-driven recommendations** to reduce delays

