| 1 | **ORD** | Chicago O'Hare | 40.51 |
| 2 | **DFW** | Dallas/Fort Worth | 36.40 |
| 3 | **ATL** | Atlanta Hartsfield-Jackson | 34.96 |
| 4 | DEN | Denver International | 28.01 |
| 5 | SFO | San Francisco International | 23.69 |
| 6 | LAX | Los Angeles International | 23.41 |
| 7 | EWR | Newark Liberty | 21.36 |
| 8 | LGA | LaGuardia, New York | 19.60 |
| 9 | MCO | Orlando International | 17.62 |
| 10 | BOS | Boston Logan | 17.35 |

> 🔴 **ORD + DFW + ATL alone = 31% of all U.S. delay minutes**, despite being < 1% of airports.

---

### 🌩️ Which Delay Cause Impacts Flights Most?

| Cause | Total Minutes (M) | Share | Nature |
|-------|------------------|-------|--------|
| **Late Aircraft** | 283.14 | **39.0%** | Operational Cascade |
| **Carrier Issues** | 246.37 | **33.9%** | Controllable |
| **NAS / ATC** | 157.82 | **21.7%** | External / Partial |
| Weather | 38.15 | 5.2% | External |
| Security | 1.27 | 0.2% | External |

> 🔑 **73% of all delays are either controllable (Carrier) or preventable (Late Aircraft cascade)**

